# Google Sheets with the second cursor: someone asks how to make a pivot table of invoices by
# customer, and the second cursor shows each step while they take it. Starts on a sheet with the
# invoices already pasted in and only A1 selected, the app running with VITE_DEMO set.
rest 1500
key alt+space
rest 900
write How do I make a pivot table of invoices by customer?
rest 600
key return
cursor think
rest 900
cursor point 311 200 Open the Insert menu.
rest 800
click 311 200
rest 400
cursor point 364 610 Choose Pivot table.
rest 800
click 364 610
cursor think
rest 700
cursor point 866 721 Keep New sheet and click Create.
rest 800
click 866 721
cursor think
rest 1900
cursor point 1087 726 Next to Rows, click Add.
rest 800
click 1087 726
rest 400
cursor point 1123 500 Pick Customer.
rest 800
click 1123 500
cursor think
rest 700
cursor say Scroll down in the editor to Values.
rest 900
move 1010 640
scroll -8
cursor think
rest 500
cursor point 1087 756 Next to Values, click Add.
rest 800
click 1087 756
rest 400
cursor point 1132 678 Pick Gross (HUF).
rest 800
click 1132 678
cursor think
rest 900
cursor done Done: every customer, with their total gross.
rest 1200
move 420 520
rest 2500
move 560 720
rest 6000
